  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.7.0 (2026-07-21):\n\n            BREAKING:\n            - Target framework is net10.0 only (dropped net9.0)\n            - RtlSdrDeviceManager.Instance no longer throws when no device is present (check CountDevices)\n            - State errors throw InvalidOperationException instead of RtlSdrLibraryExecutionException\n            - CloseAllManagedDevice() is a no-op when no devices are open\n\n            FIXED:\n            - Async callback no longer throws across the native boundary (previously crashed the process)\n            - Device instances no longer hold a permanent GCHandle self-reference (USB handle can be released)\n            - Reliable, safe async stop/dispose; requested stops are not reported as errors\n            - Console-suppression scope pairing no longer leaks stdout/stderr redirection\n            - ArgumentOutOfRangeException from device setters now carries a proper ParamName\n\n            ADDED:\n            - AsyncReadException property, RefreshDevices(), XML documentation in the package\n            - KerberosSDRMode is now settable; unit test project\n\n            See CHANGELOG.md for complete details.",
